            "old_string": "### 52.2 Identity mapping protection in SC→TC conversion\n- [ ] Related to 43.1 (multi-round pipeline) and 52.3 (ambiguous chars).\n      Inspired by `externals/zhtw` matcher.py 'protected ranges':\n      when SC→TC conversion matches a substring that is part of a\n      longer already-correct TW term, the longer term must be\n      protected from over-conversion.  Example: '演算法' is correct\n      zh-TW; a naive converter matching '算法'→'演算法' inside it\n      would produce '演演算法'.\n  - The Python zhtw project solves this with binary-search over\n    identity-mapped ranges (O(m log m) per lookup).  Our daachorse\n    AC already uses longest-match-first, which prevents most cases,\n    but the SC→TC converter in `s2t.rs` processes STPhrases →\n    STCharacters → TWVariants sequentially.  A shorter phrase match\n    in round 1 can produce text that round 2 incorrectly extends.\n  - Fix: after each conversion round, record the char-offset ranges\n    of replacements as 'protected zones' in the current output buffer.\n    Since replacements change buffer length, protected zones must be\n    tracked in the output coordinate space of each round (not the\n    input).  At each round boundary, rebuild the protected-zone set\n    from scratch on the new output buffer.  Subsequent rounds skip\n    matches that overlap any protected zone.\n  - Caution: naive whole-span protection can suppress legitimate\n    adjacent conversions.  Only protect the exact replacement range,\n    not surrounding context.\n  - Scope: `src/engine/s2t.rs` (protected zone tracking per round).\n  - Gate: round-trip test on corpus containing '演算法', '執行緒',\n    '記憶體' produces identical output.  No double-conversion on\n    any term in TWVariants.txt.  Mixed phrase+char test where text\n    adjacent to a replacement is still correctly converted.\n\n### 52.3 Ambiguous character exclusion list for SC→TC character layer",
